{
  "$comment": [
    "Maps each Capability to the HTTP route(s) that express it, so the persona",
    "matrix can exercise a capability against the real application rather than",
    "against the C# map that defines it.",
    "",
    "This file is TEST EXPECTATION, not authorization truth. Models/Staff/",
    "RoleCapabilities is the only definition of who holds what; if this file and",
    "that map disagree, the map wins and the matrix test fails.",
    "",
    "'form' is the page a POST route's antiforgery token is lifted from. A POST",
    "assertion without a valid token proves nothing (see the gate document, B4),",
    "so a persona that cannot reach the form cannot be asserted against the POST.",
    "",
    "'routes': [] means the capability has no distinct HTTP route of its own.",
    "Those need a 'noRouteReason' and are reported by the coverage test rather",
    "than silently skipped."
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "capabilities": [
    {
      "capability": "ManageExecutiveDecisions",
      "routes": [],
      "noRouteReason": "Opt-in executive decision creation and transitions require tenant-owned packs and actors. ExecutiveDecisionIntegrationTests enables the feature and tests actual HTTP writes, read-only refusals and foreign IDs."
    },
    {
      "capability": "ReviewExecutiveEvidence",
      "routes": [],
      "noRouteReason": "Opt-in evidence review requires a saved decision and version. ExecutiveDecisionIntegrationTests exercises review actions with real antiforgery and permission boundaries."
    },
